## 04.1. Browser Capability Detection

Evaluate:

```javascript
navigator.hardwareConcurrency
navigator.deviceMemory
navigator.storage?.estimate()
globalThis.crossOriginIsolated
typeof SharedArrayBuffer
typeof WebAssembly
```

Perform actual WebAssembly feature detection.

Do not assume SIMD is supported merely because WebAssembly exists.

Do not infer CPU model, AVX2 support or physical core count from User-Agent strings.

Important limitations:

- `navigator.deviceMemory` is unavailable in some browsers.
- Its value may be rounded or restricted.
- `navigator.hardwareConcurrency` is a logical concurrency hint, not a physical core count.
- Browser memory availability is not identical to installed physical RAM.
- Browser storage quotas are dynamic.
- Browser CPU capabilities are not fully exposed through standard JavaScript.

Use conservative capability estimates when detailed data is unavailable.

Unknown values must remain UNKNOWN, not zero.

All device detection must execute locally.

Do not send hardware fingerprints to a remote service.

